<figure class="lms-figure" aria-labelledby="fig-dispute">
  <figcaption id="fig-dispute" class="lms-figure-caption">A dispute, start to finish</figcaption>
  <ol class="lms-timeline">
    <li class="lms-timeline-item"><span class="lms-timeline-when">Day 0</span><span class="lms-timeline-what"><strong>The sale.</strong> Chip or tap, itemized receipt, clear name on the slip.</span></li>
    <li class="lms-timeline-item"><span class="lms-timeline-when">Up to ~120 days later</span><span class="lms-timeline-what"><strong>Customer disputes it with their bank.</strong> “I don't recognize this”, “never received”, “charged twice”, “fraud”.</span></li>
    <li class="lms-timeline-item lms-timeline-item-mark"><span class="lms-timeline-when">Notice</span><span class="lms-timeline-what"><strong>Valmar tells us.</strong> The money is taken from our account at once, plus a chargeback fee.</span></li>
    <li class="lms-timeline-item"><span class="lms-timeline-when">30 days (Visa) · 45 days (Mastercard)</span><span class="lms-timeline-what"><strong>We respond with evidence</strong> or accept it. Miss the window and it is lost.</span></li>
    <li class="lms-timeline-item"><span class="lms-timeline-when">Weeks later</span><span class="lms-timeline-what"><strong>Decision.</strong> Won: the money returns. Lost: it stays with the customer. The fee usually stays either way.</span></li>
  </ol>
</figure>
